title: FOLFIRINOX and gemcitabine-nab-paclitaxel - metastatic pancreatic cancer
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Takeaway:'' Both regimens improved first-line survival versus gemcitabine alone in metastatic pancreatic adenocarcinoma; their pivotal trials do not establish superiority over each other.
* ''PRODIGE 4/ACCORD 11 (2011):'' 342 untreated patients, ECOG performance status 0–1, age ≤75. FOLFIRINOX (fluorouracil/leucovorin, irinotecan, oxaliplatin) versus gemcitabine: median overall survival ''11.1 vs 6.8 months'' (death hazard ratio 0.57); median progression-free survival ''6.4 vs 3.3 months''; objective response ''31.6% vs 9.4%''. Greater toxicity, but definitive quality-of-life deterioration at 6 months was lower (31% vs 66%).
* ''MPACT (2013):'' 861 untreated patients, Karnofsky performance status ≥70. Gemcitabine plus nab-paclitaxel (Abraxane) versus gemcitabine: median overall survival ''8.5 vs 6.7 months'' (death hazard ratio 0.72); median progression-free survival ''5.5 vs 3.7 months''; objective response ''23% vs 7%''. Increased neuropathy and myelosuppression.
* ''Board pearl:'' Avoid comparing 11.1 versus 8.5 months across trials: eligibility differed. Original FOLFIRINOX results are not a randomized validation of every modified schedule.

Sources: [[Conroy 2011|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21561347/]]; [[Von Hoff 2013|https://doi.org/10.1056/NEJMoa1304369]]; ASCO SEP 2026, ch. 13.1, pp. 656–658; NCCN Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma v3.2026, PANC-G 5; Discussion MS-28, MS-31.
